{
    "version": "https://jsonfeed.org/version/1",
    "title": "mdn/content update content",
    "home_page_url": "https://azu.github.io/github-search-rss/mdn-content.json",
    "feed_url": "https://azu.github.io/github-search-rss/mdn-content.json",
    "description": "mdn/content update content on GitHub",
    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update all workflows using <code class=\"notranslate\">pull_request_target</code> to specify trusted target branches, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Security best practice to limit <code class=\"notranslate\">pull_request_target</code> workflows to trusted branches, reducing the attack surface for malicious pull requests.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">pull_request_target</code> trigger causes the workflow to run in the context of the base branch with access to secrets, so it's important:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>to specify <strong>only</strong> trusted branches, to avoid that the workflow runs on an untrusted branch,</li>\n<li>to specify <strong>all</strong> trusted branches, to avoid that the workflow is skipped on PRs targeting a trusted branch.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-workflows/events-that-trigger-workflows#pull_request_target\">https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-workflows/events-that-trigger-workflows#pull_request_target</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3566969685\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1021\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/1021/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1021\">mdn/fred#1021</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41741",
            "title": "ci(workflows): specify `pull_request_target` branches",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-29T17:30:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-29T17:19:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/bounce-tracking-mitigations\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bounce tracking mitigations</a> is a privacy-protecting feature available from Chromium 116 onwards, which also has support in Firefox and Safari in similar forms. It is <a href=\"https://privacycg.github.io/nav-tracking-mitigations/#bounce-tracking-mitigations\" rel=\"nofollow\">specified here</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a page explaining how it works. This is one of the privacy sandbox features that is fully released and being kept, which I hadn't gotten around to documenting.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that is is a browser feature, and not a web platform feature. As a result, it doesn't really have a sensible way to record it in BCD.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41740",
            "title": "Technical review: Add doc covering bounce tracking mitigations",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-29T16:37:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-29T16:27:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates all <code class=\"notranslate\">on: pull_request</code> workflows to run on all PRs, not just on PRs targeting <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The condition is unnecessary, and might obfuscate test failures.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3566425257\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1020\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/1020/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1020\">mdn/fred#1020</a>.</p>",
